A||N||4||black-86-GT||brakes||||1||
Z||000000||black-86-GT||04-02-2000||06:06 PM||||Ok I have a problem with my brakes. whenever I'm rolling slow say to a stop light, a parking space or driving through a parking lot. I hear this kind of sqealing sound coming from the rear of the car. the sound goes away when I apply the brakes and when I turn left. but gets louder and faster when I turn right or speed up. I have replaced the brake pads and its still doing it. Am I going to have to replace the rotor or is there something else I can do? any help would be appreciated<BR>thanx Michael Crosby||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-02-2000||07:05 PM||||If all the hardware is in good shape.<P>if the calipers are sliding like they should be, somtimes the calpiers move durring turning enough to drag a pad.<P>There's not a whole lot that can be done about it.<P>If the hardware is crappy.<P>the calipers may not be floating back to where they belong. the rear bearing pack has a certain amount of play. (it suposed to.) this can be enough to push the disk against the pad or the dust shield. Either of which could make noise. IF the dust sheild is bent it would have the same result.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroshop||04-02-2000||08:35 PM||||More then likely all you need to do is bend the dust shield behind the rotore away from the rotor. I've had to do that to more Fieros . It seems that almost the Fieros that I work on have to bend the plate back a little and walla no more squeel.||||reg||1
Z||000003||black-86-GT||04-03-2000||10:03 AM||||Yea I already know about the dust shield and have already bent it back. I talked W/ my dad about it and he said that he had that problem also but it was a bearing race that was spinning inside the hub but I dont know the car has 110K on it and I wouldnt doubt anything about now||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaveL||04-03-2000||03:04 PM||||My money says that its a wheel bearing problem. That can easily cause a squeel that starts or stops during turning certain directions. Its sure worth checking out whenever you grease and repack the bearings.<P>Good luck||||reg||1
